{
  "name": "bulk_segmentation",
  "how": "Zero-shot instance segmentation of packed soybeans on the 40 original images (aug 01) of Mechanical-harvest soybean hwdtghttp7. GT instances: palette-snapped class masks, 4-connected components per class, specks < 5 % of the median intact seed dropped, merged crushed/intact components split by distance watershed (pipeline/harvest_index.py rules, counts checked against harvest_seeds.csv). Methods: FastSAM-s (Ultralytics 8.4.194, weights v8.3.0 SHA-256 c9f78716..., CPU), Cellpose-SAM (cellpose 4.2.1.1, cpsam), segment_multi (Lab b* Otsu components, count = sum of area/median-seed estimates) and a distance-transform watershed on its foreground. Raw configs (FastSAM imgsz 640/1024/1280, retina on/off, NMS IoU .7/.9; Cellpose diameter auto/130, half resolution; watershed foreground and peak distance) and post-processing (conf threshold, drop masks > 25 % of the image, area band relative to the image's median mask, drop masks darker than a fraction of the median mask L* (gaps between seeds), greedy de-dup by IoU and containment) chosen by pooled F1 on the 28 train originals only; headline on the 6 test originals, secondary on all 40 (no method saw any of them). Matching: greedy one-to-one at IoU >= 0.5. Count error = number of kept masks (segment_multi: sum of n_est) minus GT instances (all classes; seeds only = crushed + intact). Boundary F with 3 px tolerance on matched pairs. 95 % CIs: percentile bootstrap over images. Seconds per image: model inference + post-processing, model loaded, OMP_NUM_THREADS=6 on a c7i.4xlarge shared with another job. The winner (by train F1) is also run on the 3 Ghana demo photos.",
